131, H134, R135, V136, H138","assay":"x-ray crystallography · 3D structure","note":"The epitope of ABT007 Fab on the human EPO receptor (EPOR) was determined from the crystal structure of the complex. EPOR exists as a preformed dimer, however for crystallization monomeric soluble domain of the receptor was used. The crystallographic unit [PDB: 2JIX] contains 3 EPOR monomers (chains  B, C, E), and 3 Fabs: (1) chains A (light) and F (heavy), (2) G (light) and D (heavy), and (3) L (light) and H (heavy). The Fabs interact with EPOR as follows: Fab(1) with C chain (both Fab chains contact) and B (light chain contacts only); Fab(2) with chain E (both Fab chains contact) and chain C (light chain contacts only); Fab(3) with chain E ((light chain contacts only). Since the contacts are different, two complexes were curated: Fab(1) with chain C and Fab(2) with chain E.; Unmapped quantitative response: 3D structure 3.2 angstroms","assertion_origin":"source","source_url":"https://www.iedb.org/database_export_v3.php","record_url":"http://www.iedb.org/assay/1716829","link_scope":"record","measurements":[],"target_external_id":"http://www.uniprot.org/uniprot/P19235","assay_ids":["1716829"],"receptor_group_id":"171","id":"ix_da224c797ae695ab7cd3","target_id":"target:erythropoietin-receptor-4f2e8fecfdd9","target_name":"Erythropoietin receptor"},{"antibody_id":"ab_353ff1640c3e838f9224","target_raw":"Erythropoietin receptor","relationship":"binds","evidence":"CURATED","source":"iedb","source_record_id":"171","reference":"http://www.iedb.org/reference/1018824","epitope":"E49, L50, W88, E121, R123, P131, H134, R135, V136, H138","assay":"x-ray crystallography · 3D structure","note":"The epitope of ABT007 Fab on the human EPO receptor (EPOR) was determined from the crystal structure of the complex. EPOR exists as a preformed dimer, however, monomeric soluble domain of the receptor was used for crystallization. The crystallographic unit [PDB: 2JIX] contains 3 EPOR monomers (chains  B, C, E)